        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-30T02:18:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "is it an error if someone calls registerSmsListener and mSmsListener is already nonnull? Or is the intention to possibly allow this to unlink the SmsListener as well during cleanup (by passing null)? Else suggest @NonNull on listener param.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 117,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 117,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "037749df03aff860db94c47e69b4ba3913f5e0e2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "38d0e350_c825ff61",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/ims/feature/SmsFeature.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 117,
      "author": {
        "id": 1098053
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-30T16:04:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should be a private method, actually.\n\nIt is only used by the framework once during initialization to register the listener back to the framework.\n\nWe then call onFeatureReady() after to signal to the feature that the framework has initialized everything. Any usage of the mSmsListener while it is still null should result in an exception.",
      "parentUuid": "0e2808ff_c4d5990a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 117,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 117,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "037749df03aff860db94c47e69b4ba3913f5e0e2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
