        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-30T02:18:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "suggest that rather than overriding this function we take the value in the constructor and make it final... or something? Basically, this seems (to me, who isn\u0027t a java ninja) like a weird way to have a child class provide a compile-time constant.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 211,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 213,
